{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod","id":680042,"title":"Madoka Magica in the WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-27T08:11:42-07:00","id":680042,"title":"Madoka Magica in the WoD","content":"So after watching the series and the movie I wondered what would happen if that was going on in the World of Darkness (And yes, I'm aware of Princess: the Hopeful, that's not what I'm looking for). What would happen in the Incubators and the magical girl system were active in the WoD? How would the various supernatural groups react to them? What would happen to mortals caught in web that the Incubators are spinning? Personally here's some of my thoughts:<br /> <br /> The Technocracy would take a dim view of a group of creatures creating reality deviants and wrecking the city particularly the Progenitors and Void Engineers. The former due to the fact that Incubators act almost like the vector of a plague (and the name alone is a spit in the Progenitors' faces) and the latter because it's aliens messing with humanity (and some of the crazier ones might think they have something to do with Threat Null). More compassionate Progenitors might try to free the girls from their contracts and convert them to the Technocratic paradigm. If they could accomplish this then the Incubators and the witches would have a powerfully motivated foe dedicated to getting in their way.<br /> <br /> On the Tradition side I see the Euthanatoi, Choristers, and Verbena having the biggest problem with the whole thing. The magical girl system inherently messes with the cycle the Euthanatoi espouse so most likely the Incubators (and the girls if they can't be helped) would be given the Good Death. The Choristers would see the Incubators as demons and respond accordingly while the Verbena might see the system and its end result as a perversion of what they hold sacred.<br /> <br /> I can see some demons getting into contract wars with the Incubators. Let's face it the demons can do many of things the Incubators can and they tend to have better rates than Kyubey and his ilk (Sure, Sayaka I can heal your boyfriend. The price? All you have to do is believe in me.). Then there's threatening (deliberate or not) whatever a Scourge or more guardianship minded demon is protecting.<br /> <br /> For werewolves it would mostly depend on whether the girls, witches, etc reek of Wyrm taint and whether the Incubators are targeting the wolf blooded. There's also the possibility that the Incubators' whole ridiculous plan is a trick of the Wyrm and meant to spread chaos and corruption rather than actually dealing with entropy.<br /> <br /> Dauntains might revel in the banality that witches represent and try to speed up the process for any magical girls they come across leading other changelings to try and counteract this.<br /> <br /> More crazy hunters would have little problem killing the girls but the saner ones would face a moral dilemma that would be interesting to explore.<br /> <br /> The girls themselves would likely try to destroy whatever supernatural threat appeared to them either mistaking them for witches or realizing the truth and simply deciding to protect themselves.<br /> <br /> Anyways let me know your thoughts! How so you think the other groups would react? What kind of plots would you run involving the girls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T17:44:43-07:00","id":681593,"title":"","content":"Incubators are a very fucked up Spiritual response, perhaps they are Gaian perhaps they are wyld, perhaps they are something else but just as various darker umbral types push a mage to Nephandidom this &quot;pattern&quot; is a rejection of Cosmic entropy via infusing greater creative energy into the cycle. The girls are mages. The path to Witchdom is Quiet. Incubators have been farming Marauders to bring more chaos into the world.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately Madoka's Quiet is SUPER Effective and sucks it in. And then Homura's Quiet wraps around it. So now they are trapped in the new worlds they have forged out of the trauma and madness of two girls and some of their friends.. but hey it might have beaten entropy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T18:18:48-07:00","id":681612,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Witches are blatant Marauders. They are each in their own realm of utter madness. I'd say Incubators are Pattern creatures. They harvest Marauders, but only do so so that the universe will remain utterly eternally unchanged. They want to counteract entrophy, but aren't actually pro-wyld. Wyld is just a resources to counteract entropy to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T18:46:19-07:00","id":681623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=681612#post681612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Witches are blatant Marauders. They are each in their own realm of utter madness. I'd say Incubators are Pattern creatures. They harvest Marauders, but only do so so that the universe will remain utterly eternally unchanged. They want to counteract entrophy, but aren't actually pro-wyld. Wyld is just a resources to counteract entropy to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd sya they are High Umbral entities so they don't play into the werewolf game vs being some crazy high umbral beings that harvest marauders to make new worlds because the end is coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T19:14:42-07:00","id":681659,"title":"","content":"Indeed, an interesting interpretation of the Triat, to be sure. Agents of Stasis, using Dynamism to combat Entropy. All the while sowing discord.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of The Spirit Ways (yes, I know it isn't a very good book), with some Shamans Awakened and instructed in magic by spirits. I can see the Incubators as powerful Umbrood that saw the sorry state of reality, and made it their mission to avert the heat death. But while they're capable of playing themselves off as good and even set up their system to &quot;help&quot; their &quot;clients&quot;, they're ultimately looking out for their interests. They don't really care for magical girls, save as a resource.<br /> <br /> They're also very much like Demons, except what they want are bountiful emotional energy, in the form of both Hope and Despair. They don't quite understand what these are, just that they are powerful sources of (Quintessential) energy. So they make contracts with little girls - they are the ones most vulnerable to the pitch, after all - providing them with magic and a few...let's call them Investments, perhaps. Or perhaps not.<br /> <br /> After thinking about it, the magical girls themselves would probably need to be Mages, rather than just Sorcerers with a few select Paths and some Incubator Investments (or Blessings, mixed though they are). For one, Magical Girls in Madoka Magica are capable of seeing Witches and their minions, so they need to have Awakened sight. It would be slightly silly for one to be able to see the unseen and yet not have the wool pulled from their eyes. They can also shift into Witch dens, which at the very least are some sort of pocket realm or Marauder bubble of altered reality. If the Witches are just magical girls gone Maraud, one would need to be Awakened so as not to be pulled into their version of reality and think of it as perfectly normal.<br /> <br /> And of course, Magical Girls have a built-in mechanism for handling Paradox: their darkening gems. Of course these Soul Gems would naturally be Phylacteries, containing the magical girl's Avatar. But these would be specially enchanted by the Incubators so that the Paradox these girls (or boys, if we're altering things) accrue, instead of being released in backlash, instead collects in their gem. And the only way they can remove the Paradox is to kill Witches - Magical Girls whose gems became too stained with Paradox and were shunted all at once into stage 6 Quiet. They must claim the gems-turned-grief-seeds and shunt Paradox onto them.<br /> <br /> Well, that or employ some sort of Prime Effect to disperse the Paradox or force a backlash. Or just park their Soul Gems at a Node, and let the Paradox bleed off. But of course, the Incubators don't tell the Magical Girls that this is possible. To do that would be to potentially break the cycle of Hope and Despair, and allow the girls to go free. And the Incubators can't have that. It's why the Incubators work closely with their charges, guiding their development so that their Paradigms never slip beyond what the Incubators tell the Magical Girls is possible. Never allow them to know the Truth: that the Magical Girls are really Mages, people capable of altering reality as they please. That Reality itself causes their gems to darken as a result of showy, impossible displays. That they can massively extend their lives - perhaps indefinitely - simply by keeping their magic subtle. And that all of this was deliberately engineered by the Incubators to push the girls towards witch-dom. <br /> <br /> But if a magical girl did learn the truth...if they met other Mages who could teach them what they really are...oh, what a reckoning would their be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T19:59:54-07:00","id":681695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=681659#post681659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, an interesting interpretation of the Triat, to be sure. Agents of Stasis, using Dynamism to combat Entropy. All the while sowing discord.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel like Incubators are Middle Umbral so I don't think they fall solidly into the Triat pattern, To compare there are 3 types of Nephandi, Infernalists, Malfeans, and K'laaasha. Malfeans actively serve the Middle Umbral wyrm. Infernalists serve High umbral &quot;demons&quot; and K'aassha serve wierd cthulhu things that don't fall quite into the setup. I Imagine the Incubators are some High Umbral entity or maybe true outsiders who will do anything to escape the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T15:12:42-07:00","id":682376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=681659#post681659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, an interesting interpretation of the Triat, to be sure. Agents of Stasis, using Dynamism to combat Entropy. All the while sowing discord.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of The Spirit Ways (yes, I know it isn't a very good book), with some Shamans Awakened and instructed in magic by spirits. I can see the Incubators as powerful Umbrood that saw the sorry state of reality, and made it their mission to avert the heat death. But while they're capable of playing themselves off as good and even set up their system to &quot;help&quot; their &quot;clients&quot;, they're ultimately looking out for their interests. They don't really care for magical girls, save as a resource.<br /> <br /> They're also very much like Demons, except what they want are bountiful emotional energy, in the form of both Hope and Despair. They don't quite understand what these are, just that they are powerful sources of (Quintessential) energy. So they make contracts with little girls - they are the ones most vulnerable to the pitch, after all - providing them with magic and a few...let's call them Investments, perhaps. Or perhaps not.<br /> <br /> After thinking about it, the magical girls themselves would probably need to be Mages, rather than just Sorcerers with a few select Paths and some Incubator Investments (or Blessings, mixed though they are). For one, Magical Girls in Madoka Magica are capable of seeing Witches and their minions, so they need to have Awakened sight. It would be slightly silly for one to be able to see the unseen and yet not have the wool pulled from their eyes. They can also shift into Witch dens, which at the very least are some sort of pocket realm or Marauder bubble of altered reality. If the Witches are just magical girls gone Maraud, one would need to be Awakened so as not to be pulled into their version of reality and think of it as perfectly normal.<br /> <br /> And of course, Magical Girls have a built-in mechanism for handling Paradox: their darkening gems. Of course these Soul Gems would naturally be Phylacteries, containing the magical girl's Avatar. But these would be specially enchanted by the Incubators so that the Paradox these girls (or boys, if we're altering things) accrue, instead of being released in backlash, instead collects in their gem. And the only way they can remove the Paradox is to kill Witches - Magical Girls whose gems became too stained with Paradox and were shunted all at once into stage 6 Quiet. They must claim the gems-turned-grief-seeds and shunt Paradox onto them.<br /> <br /> Well, that or employ some sort of Prime Effect to disperse the Paradox or force a backlash. Or just park their Soul Gems at a Node, and let the Paradox bleed off. But of course, the Incubators don't tell the Magical Girls that this is possible. To do that would be to potentially break the cycle of Hope and Despair, and allow the girls to go free. And the Incubators can't have that. It's why the Incubators work closely with their charges, guiding their development so that their Paradigms never slip beyond what the Incubators tell the Magical Girls is possible. Never allow them to know the Truth: that the Magical Girls are really Mages, people capable of altering reality as they please. That Reality itself causes their gems to darken as a result of showy, impossible displays. That they can massively extend their lives - perhaps indefinitely - simply by keeping their magic subtle. And that all of this was deliberately engineered by the Incubators to push the girls towards witch-dom.<br /> <br /> But if a magical girl did learn the truth...if they met other Mages who could teach them what they really are...oh, what a reckoning would their be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so would it be possible to break the connection between the girl and the soul gem and if so how? I would assume it would involve a decent understanding of Spirit. As far as many of the effects magical girls use I'm assuming most of them would be favoring Forces, Correspondence, and Matter with a few oddballs like Homura focusing on Time, Life, and Spirit with maybe a few going full Nanoha and developing their own weird technocratic flavor of those spheres.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:50:43-07:00","id":682442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=682376#post682376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, so would it be possible to break the connection between the girl and the soul gem and if so how? I would assume it would involve a decent understanding of Spirit. As far as many of the effects magical girls use I'm assuming most of them would be favoring Forces, Correspondence, and Matter with a few oddballs like Homura focusing on Time, Life, and Spirit with maybe a few going full Nanoha and developing their own weird technocratic flavor of those spheres.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Avatar is in the Soul Gem. To break the connection would be gigul. I'd imagine Spirit and mind might be &quot;forbidden' spheres for this craft","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:02:35-07:00","id":682497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=682442#post682442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Avatar is in the Soul Gem. To break the connection would be gigul. I'd imagine Spirit and mind might be &quot;forbidden' spheres for this craft</div> </div> </div> </div>So what about drawing the Avatar out of the soul gem and reattaching it to the girl's body? I'd assume that would require a high level of Spirit and Mind, possibly even Correspondence as well to relink the Avatar with the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:28:10-07:00","id":682530,"title":"","content":"My view of Mage is that anything is possible with the Sphere system, so long as enough successes are rolled. That being said, is it entirely necessary to remove a magical girl's Avatar from the Soul gem? Their current state would provide ample justification for the Phylactery Flaw, because in Madoka Magica, that is exactly what the Soul Gem is. The important point would be figuring out how to alter the Soul Gem so that it would no longer soak up the magical girl's Paradox, until it reached critical mass and turned them into a Marauder. In that case, we're probably looking at a high level Prime/Matter/Spirit Effect.<br /> <br /> Then again, that assumes the Incubators designed the Soul Gems to do that. It could very well be that there's little or nothing special about these Phylacteries. Rather, the accumulation of Paradox in the gems is a result of the magical girls' belief. The Incubators told them that every time they use their magic, their gems get a little darker. As the Technocracy has shown, Paradox backlashes tend to conform in some manner to a Mage's beliefs. Technocrats see their devices break down and blame &quot;impurities of a non-sterile environment&quot;. Old school Artisans would blame the break-down of their machines in the hands of the unAwakened as the result of poor maintenance. A Chorister's backlash might take the form of spontaneous stigmata, etc.<br /> <br /> Given that the Incubators would try to prevent their charges from receiving any outside ideas, it could very well be that the effect is entirely a result of a magical girl's ignorance of what Paradox is and what it means.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that Incubators in Madoka Magica don't really understand why magic works. They are playing with forces that confound them, but which they grasp just enough to exploit. While an Incubator might be able to pull a magical girl's Avatar from their body and plug it into a prepared vessel, that doesn't mean they'd be able to tinker with it enough to add extra features. They might not know how to make Paradox collect in the gem, just know that it can be made to so long as the subject is made to believe it is so. I can just imagine them experimenting, probably over years, until they stumble on a method for guiding magical girls towards Quiet. This is why they keep the magical girls ignorant, so that they fight witches, preferably never realizing that they too will become witches if they stay the course the Kyubeys set for them.<br /> <br /> It changes the magical girl's existence from an inevitable and tragic cycle into a problem that can be overcome, so long as the girls have the Will to impress their own reality on things. Something that Mage is all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T19:42:29-07:00","id":682590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=682530#post682530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It changes the magical girl's existence from an inevitable and tragic cycle into a problem that can be overcome, so long as the girls have the Will to impress their own reality on things. Something that Mage is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that what Madoka and Homura did in canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T19:42:31-07:00","id":682591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=682530#post682530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It changes the magical girl's existence from an inevitable and tragic cycle into a problem that can be overcome, so long as the girls have the Will to impress their own reality on things. Something that Mage is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there is evidence to support this in one of the movies though it did require a tremendous of power from what amounted to at least some kind of archmage as well as the insane will of someone who was a step away from becoming a Marauder to accomplish. Still, it did happen. Now as for as ditching the Soul Gem goes it depends on the goal: If the girl wants to go back to &quot;normal&quot; then they're going to want to be able to get rid of the Soul Gem. Others might want to keep it around.<br /> <br /> That's a good note about the Incubators; they're playing with forces they don't understand and that's likely to blow up in their faces someday. If a magical girl figured out a way to &quot;purify&quot; and &quot;enhance&quot; the magical girl template then they could potentially become more than the Incubators can handle. I'm willing to bet that their view of their process is completely wrong and that the creation of a witch is wreaking havoc with the dimensional fabric and possibly directly affecting neighboring dimensions such as pissing off ghosts and the like. At the very least the resonance from energy pulled from mages going insane can't be all that good and may well be affecting their species.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T23:18:40-07:00","id":682689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=682591#post682591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now as for as ditching the Soul Gem goes it depends on the goal: If the girl wants to go back to &quot;normal&quot; then they're going to want to be able to get rid of the Soul Gem. Others might want to keep it around.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a certain value of &quot;normal&quot;, yes.<br /> <br /> But yes, I can fully see the Incubators unknowingly causing considerable harm, while simultaneously doing nothing to actually halt Entropy. Eating a grief seed loaded with despair-flavored Paradox can't be healthy either.<br /> <br /> Heck, we could play with that. Let's say that the Incubators actually have been around for a while in WoD, granting little girls' wishes and giving them magic powers. And originally they were, if not precisely good, than not particularly evil. But every time they absorbed a spent grief seed, their collective became darker. Then they slowly started seeing no reason not to engineer the falls of their charges. After all, making more of them go Witch afforded the Kyubeys more energy to feast on. Which in turn made the Kyubey more corrupt. I still don't see their operation running for more than a few centuries, but that'd be more than enough time to become a potentially dark force. All while fully believing in the rightness and necessity of their mission.<br /> <br /> And every time, making more magical girls and encouraging them towards more battles, more activity, more showy magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T04:52:38-07:00","id":682973,"title":"","content":"I would argue given CWOD metaphysics Madoka and Homura are not fail states for the incubators plans but rather close to their win condition. Sufficient levels of Quiet basically cause a Marauder to fall out of the Universe. That's basically what Madoka and Homura do they grab everyone create theirown universe and fuck the rest of the world. That I think is the ultimate plan use a Marauder as the seed of a new universe where everything isn't fucked up and broken.<br /> <br /> Of course the incubators have a limited understanding of the situation since Ascension seems to be an equally valid direction but this is clearly easier and more reproduceable!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:34:23-07:00","id":683604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=682973#post682973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue given CWOD metaphysics Madoka and Homura are not fail states for the incubators plans but rather close to their win condition. Sufficient levels of Quiet basically cause a Marauder to fall out of the Universe. That's basically what Madoka and Homura do they grab everyone create theirown universe and fuck the rest of the world. That I think is the ultimate plan use a Marauder as the seed of a new universe where everything isn't fucked up and broken.<br /> <br /> Of course the incubators have a limited understanding of the situation since Ascension seems to be an equally valid direction but this is clearly easier and more reproduceable!</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the Incubators basically say after Madoka's Ascension and their little stunt with Homura that the witch system is preferable due to the amount of energy that is given off when one is created. Similarly I doubt that they intended to get enslaved and mind raped by an angry demon with a grudge. Ultimately Madoka and Homura were the last thing they would consider a win condition as not only do they not get the energy they seek but now their plans are royally borked one way or another. The big problem with the Incubators is that they have enough knowledge (and thus rope) to hang themselves with and no common sense (read compassion) to know when they're about to jump off the cliff. Inevitably the witch system was going to go horribly wrong for them.<br /> <br /> Now I could easily see minions of the Wyrm or Nephandi setting up the Incubators to find out about this emotional energies knowing that with their entirely logic and efficiency based outlook would lead them to go buck wild and try to collect as much of that energy as they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T18:28:58-07:00","id":683689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=683604#post683604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that the Incubators basically say after Madoka's Ascension and their little stunt with Homura that the witch system is preferable due to the amount of energy that is given off when one is created. Similarly I doubt that they intended to get enslaved and mind raped by an angry demon with a grudge. Ultimately Madoka and Homura were the last thing they would consider a win condition as not only do they not get the energy they seek but now their plans are royally borked one way or another. The big problem with the Incubators is that they have enough knowledge (and thus rope) to hang themselves with and no common sense (read compassion) to know when they're about to jump off the cliff. Inevitably the witch system was going to go horribly wrong for them.<br /> <br /> Now I could easily see minions of the Wyrm or Nephandi setting up the Incubators to find out about this emotional energies knowing that with their entirely logic and efficiency based outlook would lead them to go buck wild and try to collect as much of that energy as they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>canon Madoka isn't set in the CWoD. Canon madoka is about using the system to counter act the impersonal but inevitable decay of all things. Cwod entropy isn't impersonal. Its Crazy and Hates you. Witches don't just naturally fall out of the universe if driven crazy enough in canon, in Mage metaphysics enough Quiet will cause them to just fall out. The shard that allows for someone to do magic may be either a piece of the creator or a replication of such. Entropy isn't some far off cold death of the universe billions of years from now in CWod, the end is coming and soon.<br /> <br /> With these things in mind I am adapting Madoka canon to fit the CWod Metaphysics. Now the incubators could be working with limited data and are trying to fix the triatic imbalance by coldly and calmly throwing more chaos into the system until it breaks and cancels the whole setup. I am working from the assumption that while they have have limited understanding of humanity and magic they might have a superior spiritual understanding. With this in mind its clear humans can escape the system(Ascension, Quiet) perhaps the system is hopelessly broken and escape is the only real option.<br /> <br /> Now Homura and Madoka in these premises are bad successes. Its the ultimate goal but with them having completely lost control","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T19:22:31-07:00","id":683753,"title":"","content":"Then again, in cWoD Madoka and Homura wouldn't have gotten as far as they did. The Contract system in the series worked however it wanted, so was basically a plot device. You could legitimately have Madoka becoming a goddess of Hope and Homura a devil. In cWoD, we'd be looking at Madoka as Mage and Homura as Mage. Capable of incredible power, yes, but not to the point they have in Madoka Magica. Or at the very least, they're transformations would take a drastically different form: Madoka as achieving Ascension, and Homura Descending into Nephandism. Important in their own right, but not game-changing. It's very much that the Incubators see these happenings as...interesting, but irrelevant to their plans.<br /> <br /> Or at least until Nephandi Homura starts plotting their downfall. Maybe. It's one of those things that change the rules so much between original and adaptation that it's hard to get a bead on how things would play out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T20:11:26-07:00","id":683819,"title":"","content":"See, I doubt the Incubators would have much in the way of spiritual knowledge simply because if they did it would be easy to see just how messed up the WoD is spiritually but also they should be able to deduce the spiritual effects of the witch system itself which let's face it would not be pretty and would most likely force them to use a different method since you know causing a bunch of mages to go crazy would among other things attract all kinds of unclean spirits such as Banes and various madness spirits. At best I think their spiritual understanding matches that of what mages have and certainly doesn't extend to what the Garou know about the situation (i.e. they don't know the Triatic exists much less what each represents).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T23:00:15-07:00","id":683959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=683753#post683753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, in cWoD Madoka and Homura wouldn't have gotten as far as they did. The Contract system in the series worked however it wanted, so was basically a plot device. You could legitimately have Madoka becoming a goddess of Hope and Homura a devil. In cWoD, we'd be looking at Madoka as Mage and Homura as Mage. Capable of incredible power, yes, but not to the point they have in Madoka Magica. Or at the very least, they're transformations would take a drastically different form: Madoka as achieving Ascension, and Homura Descending into Nephandism. Important in their own right, but not game-changing. It's very much that the Incubators see these happenings as...interesting, but irrelevant to their plans.<br /> <br /> Or at least until Nephandi Homura starts plotting their downfall. Maybe. It's one of those things that change the rules so much between original and adaptation that it's hard to get a bead on how things would play out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's nothing Nephandic about Homura except visuals. she isn't about decay, breakdown or destruction. if this were Nwod discussion she'd be an Exarch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T23:51:03-07:00","id":683996,"title":"","content":"But she IS a perversion of the natural order, a bastardization of what a Magical Girl is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T12:27:07-07:00","id":684728,"title":"","content":"Nah I can't really see Homura as a Nephandi, it goes too much against both her personality and how she used her abilities. If anything I would see her as a mage who suctioned off some juice from a deity/spirit/ascended mage in order to become an obsessed archmage focused on delivering karmic judgement to those she feels deserves it.<br /> <br /> So how would some of the odder groups in WoD react to the magical girls? Changelings, demons, wraiths, kuei-jin, mummies, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T14:16:57-07:00","id":684861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=683996#post683996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But she IS a perversion of the natural order, a bastardization of what a Magical Girl is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So is Madoka in the anime. She litterally shatters the natural order of corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T15:33:07-08:00","id":768141,"title":"","content":"Homura is a more of a Marauder really. Especially when you consider her universe-wide reality bubble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T16:05:51-08:00","id":770356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/680042-madoka-magica-in-the-wod?p=768141#post768141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homura is a more of a Marauder really. Especially when you consider her universe-wide reality bubble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of sort of. It's like Homura at the end of Rebellion and Madoka at the end of the series are some kind of ascended marauders that have somehow retained some of their sanity and have full control over their personal realities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}